#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119567 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/id #uuid "ba897e22-8104-5772-a0d3-9b062f3592f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4932" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $P(-3,2,1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}= \\langle 0, 2, 0 \\rangle.$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $P$ is $\\mathbf{p}=\\langle -3,2,1 \\rangle$ and $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 0,2,0 \\rangle$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes through the point $P(x_0,y_0,z_0)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $\\mathbf{n}$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(\\mathbf{r} - \\mathbf{p}) \\cdot \\mathbf{n} = 0,\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{r}$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $\\mathbf p$ is the position vector of $P.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-p\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =⟨-3,2,1⟩\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,2,0⟩ & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119568 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b0d93156-f9be-5e6e-976a-bef30dc892ee" :knowledge-point/title "Finding a Vector That Is Parallel To a Plane"}] :question/id #uuid "a33f6c43-4e25-5d67-9f73-ca99a18fb434" :question/math-academy-id "e-4933" :question/problem "A nonzero vector $\\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{b}, \\: \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{c} \\rangle$ is parallel to the plane $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3.$ What is the value of $\\dfrac{b}{c}?$" :question/worked-solution "We need a vector $\\mathbf{v} = \\langle t_1,t_2,t_3 \\rangle$ that is parallel to the given plane. \n\nFrom the equation $\\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle  = 3$ of the plane, we get the normal vector $\\mathbf{n}=\\langle 2, -1, 4 \\rangle.$ So, $\\mathbf{v} \\perp \\mathbf{n}$ and we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}v\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ ⟨{t}_{1},{t}_{2},{t}_{3}⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =0 \\\\ 2{t}_{1}-{t}_{2}+4{t}_{3} & =0 \\\\ {t}_{2} & =2{t}_{1}+4{t}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v}=\\langle t_1, 2t_1 + 4t_3, t_3 \\rangle,\n$$\n\nwhere $t_1,t_3 \\in (-\\infty,\\infty).$ \n\nWe are told that the first component of $\\mathbf{v}$ equals $0.$ So, we must set $t_1=0.$ \n\nSince $\\mathbf{v}$ is nonzero, we can pick any $t_3 \\neq 0.$ For example, setting $t_3=1$, we get\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\langle 0,\\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{4}, \\, \\bbox[2pt,Gainsboro]{1} \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $\\dfrac{b}{c} = 4.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119569 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/id #uuid "43586a83-879c-5caf-9063-a8f4afbb8b4c" :question/math-academy-id "e-4935" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(\\sqrt{2},0,-5)$ and is perpendicular to the line\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=3 \\\\ y=-1+\\sqrt{3}t \\\\ z=5-t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $\\mathbf{q}=\\langle \\sqrt{2},0,-5 \\rangle.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14042677/assets/4c70e51d85874e5a241a5d9b35b147500d4c306187c5e0a1d15a48a9aef07706.png)\n\nThe direction vector of the line is $\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1\\rangle,$ so a normal vector to the plane is \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{n}=\\mathbf{v}=\\langle  0 , \\sqrt{3} , -1 \\rangle.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =⟨\\sqrt{2},0,-5⟩\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨0,\\sqrt{3},-1⟩ & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316917 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43c7d742-9499-5f29-91d2-b9920fb9a36c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316919} {:answer/id #uuid "d65e7cbe-fab5-5020-ae76-91046be0e73a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 4 \\\\ -3\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316920} {:answer/id #uuid "e76958a4-f0a9-564b-b572-e6bb6c971a20" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316921} {:answer/id #uuid "83cfbb99-4e21-5151-9ce0-5c9a0b8bd96a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316922} {:answer/id #uuid "a7902d5d-7344-529d-a001-8ae963229f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316923}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a7902d5d-7344-529d-a001-8ae963229f7d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]=-9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316923} :answer-field/id #uuid "35db1012-2955-55e0-8997-945a65a2c3e5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316918}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "36530b79-821b-5731-b1ff-cff3103bd6a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-33027" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(1,2,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}].$" :question/worked-solution "First, note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]$ and $n=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\ r\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -4 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] & =-9.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316931 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "3f5c9c30-1745-5986-b116-e9e70a7c6161" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "72a19bb8-0aca-580c-afa4-03b4ac9e35f3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,2,2⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316933} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1fe646-46cf-51c7-9b0e-f0d83b96bee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316934} {:answer/id #uuid "732176b2-44ae-5a70-b2eb-af7b8907e33d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨3,3,2⟩=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316935} {:answer/id #uuid "5376dab4-36c0-5cb9-9c8a-6145e85d5897" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=⟨3,2,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316936} {:answer/id #uuid "17400030-8ff4-574f-b581-15a6623c0e17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,3,3⟩=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316937}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae1fe646-46cf-51c7-9b0e-f0d83b96bee6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316934} :answer-field/id #uuid "e6216fdb-ceae-536b-bdf2-c5cf55b5a6b9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045463 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a59a738a-2841-5e3f-b750-020d46e95380" :question/math-academy-id "q-33312" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that contains the point $Q(3,2,2)$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n=⟨2,2,3⟩.$" :question/worked-solution "First, notice that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨3,2,2⟩,$ $n=⟨2,2,3⟩$ is normal to the plane.\n\nThe equation of the plane that passes though the point $Q({x}_{0},{y}_{0},{z}_{0})$ and is perpendicular to the vector $n$ can be given as\n\n$$\n(r-q)\\cdot n=0,\n$$\n\nwhere $r$ is the position vector of any point on the plane, and $q$ is the position vector of $Q.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =⟨3,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨2,2,3⟩ & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316973 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "295f1e58-4a16-5d5a-b676-984818a41fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316975} {:answer/id #uuid "7c31152e-66dd-5fe9-9562-96be7263d661" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=⟨1,1,1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316976} {:answer/id #uuid "4ea2f177-4c47-5d19-aa6d-d0bf73033d47" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=⟨2,1,-1⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316977} {:answer/id #uuid "e4b58dd1-3b24-551d-b476-8762f33d28b0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,-1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316978} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd83c0d-0368-5584-91e4-39648a268e3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316979}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "295f1e58-4a16-5d5a-b676-984818a41fed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩=2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316975} :answer-field/id #uuid "475d5cee-306a-5cd5-b998-795c7327de73" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316974}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045465 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "be607052-6286-5c45-a7b0-2a7d8e65a24b" :question/math-academy-id "q-70892" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-1)$ and is perpendicular to the line that goes through the points \n$A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1).$" :question/worked-solution "First, we note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-1⟩.$\n\nSince the line  passes through the points $A(2,1,0)$ and $B(3,2,1)$ we can find a vector parallel to the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{AB} & =⟨3,2,1⟩-⟨2,1,0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,1,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nSo, a normal vector to the plane is $n=⟨1,1,1⟩.$ \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =⟨2,1,-1⟩\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,1,1⟩ & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186316980 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "45cdbb0d-2986-5c05-8d23-dce29363051b" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Vector Equation of the Plane Perpendicular to a Given Straight Line"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d60438d6-b5d2-5d15-a6df-28caf621fd6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=⟨1,-1,2⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316982} {:answer/id #uuid "1a565adb-24d5-50e4-bd12-79c885a09448" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨2,1,3⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316983} {:answer/id #uuid "8f485774-81e4-5a79-8ff4-16967d44158f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=⟨2,1,-3⟩" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316984} {:answer/id #uuid "6e428b4b-90f7-5cf9-9afd-0db57fee9352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316985} {:answer/id #uuid "9d342947-b3e8-545a-9175-0c68e2ab18bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316986}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6e428b4b-90f7-5cf9-9afd-0db57fee9352" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=-5" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316985} :answer-field/id #uuid "427df2f4-3901-5a58-af18-9a4b43dba7bb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186316981}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045464 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "836af849-3232-5f71-9fa9-a73d0d879982" :question/math-academy-id "q-70894" :question/problem "Find an equation of the plane that passes through the point $Q(2,1,-3)$ and is  perpendicular to the line \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Note that the position vector of $Q$ is $q=⟨2,1,-3⟩.$ Converting the parametric equations of the line to vector form, we get\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1+t \\\\ y=2-t \\\\ z=3+2t\\end{aligned}\\,⇒\\,⟨x,y,z⟩=⟨1,2,3⟩+t\\text{ }{{⟨1,-1,2⟩}_{⏟}}_{v}.\n$$\n\n   \n\nThe direction vector of the line is $v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.$ So, a normal  vector to the plane is \n\n$$\nn=v=⟨1,-1,2⟩.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-q)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n-q\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ r\\cdot n & =q\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =⟨2,1,-3⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
